The guest emulation conversion layer gains its arm64 forms (aarch64 port, tasks A8, D4)

The arch-guarded half of darling PR 1753`s xnu emulation delta: the tid-keyed TSD table
(tls.c/.h, the D4 mechanism), the signal-exception conversion (sigexc.c), the arm64 Linux
stat layout (stat/common.c/.h -- arm64 has no struct stat64 and a different asm-generic
field order), the sigaction conversion, the fast syscall path gate (base.h), and the
aarch64 O_DIRECTORY/O_NOFOLLOW/O_LARGEFILE values (open.h -- aarch64 overrides them in
asm/fcntl.h). Every hunk is #if/#elif __aarch64__ guarded, so x86 preprocessing is
unchanged. The PR`s new-syscall and behavioral changes (mremap_encrypted, sysctl_machdep,
the network and bsdthread pieces) are deliberately excluded: they alter the frozen x86
build and add files the generated header globs do not know.

